              "textField": "All through our lives there is a breakdown and reformation of bone, to help replace old bone. *Osteoclasts* are very large multi-nucleated cells that degrade older portions of the bone, allowing the calcium and phosphorus to circulate in general circulation. *Osteoblasts* are the bone rebuilding cells that build up the bone in areas that have been degraded by the osteoclasts. In general, for the first 30 years of a person’s life there is an overall *increase* in bone density, while after the age of 30 there is a gradual *decrease* in bone density."
            },
            "library": "H5P.DragText 1.10",
